WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Have you ever tried BBQ on BBQ? Picture this. Freshly prepared crispy seasoned chicken that's tossed in a smoky barbecue glaze and topped with a creamy barbecue sauce. Can't picture it? Well you can try it now at Tim's. Get our new BBQ crispy chicken loaded bowls and wraps for a limited time. It was Wednesday the 2nd of August 1989. 41 year old Marguerite Edwards started the day like any other, making sure her three daughters were up and ready for school. Marguerite was happily married to Ian Edwards, a successful orthodontist with a surgery in Bondi. They lived in a two story house on Victoria Road, Wallara, in Sydney's eastern suburbs. Wallara is an extremely affluent suburb, five kilometres east of Sydney's CBD, a few miles, known for its quiet treeline streets and extremely expensive housing. After getting her daughters organised, Marguerite dropped them off at Ascom School. She then made her way to an aerobics class before doing some shopping at Bondi. She then returned to her Wallara home sometime after midday. Later that afternoon Marguerite's three daughters were waiting. School had finished and they were wondering where mum was. When Marguerite didn't show up to the school that afternoon, it was very unusual. Many of the other parents even commented saying don't worry, your mum is never late. She will be here soon. But she never arrived. The girls next door neighbour Marcia Osborne ended up giving them a lift home. Marcia telling them obviously something important had come up and everything would be fine.
你试过在烧烤上再加烧烤吗？想象一下：新鲜烹制的酥脆调味鸡肉，裹上烟熏烧烤釉，再淋上一层奶油烧烤酱。想象不出来？那你现在就可以去Tim's尝尝。限时供应我们全新的烧烤脆皮鸡肉碗和卷饼。那是1989年8月2日，星期三。41岁的玛格丽特·爱德华兹像往常一样开始了一天，确保她的三个女儿起床并准备好去上学。玛格丽特与伊恩·爱德华兹婚姻幸福，伊恩是一位成功的牙齿矫正医生，在邦迪开了一家诊所。他们住在悉尼东郊沃拉拉维多利亚路上的一栋两层楼房里。沃拉拉是一个极其富裕的郊区，位于悉尼中央商务区以东五公里处，以安静的绿树成荫的街道和极其昂贵的住房而闻名。安顿好女儿们后，玛格丽特送她们去了阿斯科姆学校。然后她去上了一节健美操课，之后在邦迪买了一些东西。中午过后不久，她回到了沃拉拉的家中。那天下午晚些时候，玛格丽特的三个女儿在等待。学校放学了，她们想知道妈妈在哪里。玛格丽特那天下午没有出现在学校，这非常不寻常。许多其他家长甚至评论说，别担心，你妈妈从不迟到。她很快就会到的。但她一直没有出现。隔壁邻居玛西娅·奥斯本最终开车送她们回家。玛西娅告诉她们，显然是有什么重要的事情耽搁了，一切都会好起来的。

2
00:02:18.000 --> 00:03:56.000
But the girls had a feeling something wasn't right. When they got home, they saw Marguerite's car parked in the driveway. They walked inside and called out for their mum, but got no reply. As they slowly made their way to the kitchen, they saw a pool of blood on the floor, blood on the bench, blood on the fridge and that chairs had been knocked over. Realising something was horribly wrong, Marcia grabbed the girls and said let's get out of here, I'll ring the police. Police arrived soon after and found Marguerite's body upstairs, laying in her walk-in wardrobe, connected to the main bedroom. She had extensive head injuries and one of Ian's neck ties was wrapped around her neck. Another neck tie had been used to gag her. Detectives and specialist crime scene police were immediately called in and a forensic examination was conducted. No fingerprints were found, however they did find a towel with blood stains on it. It was 1989 and DNA analysis had only started in NSW that year. So there was no large database to compare the sample to and the nature of the testing was very different to what exists today. However it was possible that it would come in useful in the future to compare to a suspect if one was ever identified. It was clear from the forensic examination that the initial attack occurred downstairs, after which Marguerite was taken upstairs to the bedroom.
但女孩们有一种不祥的预感。当她们回到家时，看到玛格丽特的车停在车道上。她们走进屋里，大声呼唤妈妈，但没有得到回应。当她们慢慢走向厨房时，看到地板上有一滩血，长凳上有血，冰箱上有血，椅子也被撞倒了。意识到出了大事，玛西娅抓住女孩们说，我们离开这里，我去报警。警察很快赶到，在主卧室相连的步入式衣橱里发现了玛格丽特的尸体。她头部受了重伤，脖子上缠着伊恩的一条领带。另一条领带被用来堵住她的嘴。侦探和专门的犯罪现场警察立即被召集，并进行了法医检查。没有发现指纹，但他们确实发现了一条沾有血迹的毛巾。那是1989年，DNA分析那一年才在新南威尔士州开始。因此，没有大型数据库来比对样本，而且测试的性质与今天存在很大差异。然而，如果将来确定了嫌疑人，它可能会派上用场。从法医检查中可以清楚地看出，最初的袭击发生在楼下，之后玛格丽特被带到了楼上的卧室。

3
00:03:56.000 --> 00:05:03.000
She was struck to the head repeatedly with what the forensic pathologist believed was a small hammer or similar tool. The injuries were extensive, causing a fractured skull and brain damage. But the cause of death was strangulation. There was no sign of forced entry to the house. Did Marguerite know her killer and let them in? When they retraced Marguerite's steps they found that she attended an aerobics class between 10.30am and 11.30am at the nearby suburb of Bondi. She was then seen shopping also at Bondi around midday. So that raised the possibility of another theory. Marguerite was known to leave the door open while she was bringing in the shopping, was her killer waiting and simply walked in behind her. Two witnesses were identified early on, both heard screams coming from the house. One was a building surveyor who looked in the direction of the house when he heard the screams, but when he didn't see anything he got in his car and drove off.
她的头部被反复击打，法医病理学家认为凶器是一把小锤子或类似的工具。伤势严重，导致颅骨骨折和脑损伤。但死因是勒死。房子没有强行闯入的迹象。玛格丽特认识凶手并让他们进来的吗？当他们重溯玛格丽特的行踪时，发现她在上午10点30分到11点30分之间在附近的邦迪郊区参加了健美操课。中午左右，她又被看到在邦迪购物。这引发了另一种理论的可能性。众所周知，玛格丽特在搬运购物时会把门开着，是不是凶手在等她，然后直接跟在她身后走了进去？早期确定了两名目击者，他们都听到了从房子里传来的尖叫声。其中一人是一名建筑测量师，他听到尖叫声时朝房子的方向看去，但什么也没看到，于是上了车开车走了。

4
00:05:03.000 --> 00:06:09.000
The second was a woman who was walking past the house with her child. She heard screams about 1.30pm but decided not to report it as she believed it to be just another domestic. She kept walking completely ignoring what she had heard. When Ian asked the police if he could have Marguerite's jewellery back, there was no jewellery to give him. She regularly wore a diamond ring and a watch, but the killer had taken it. The ring alone was worth $20,000. It looked like a robbery had gone wrong. Marguerite had no enemies, so it was the only thing that seemed to make sense. It made even more sense when police learnt that extensive renovations had been carried out in the family home over the last few years. Ian wasn't able to offer much assistance with exactly who was hired, as Marguerite handled all of that while he was at work. So did one of the tradesmen like what he saw inside the house and decide to come back.
第二个人是一位带着孩子路过房子的妇女。她在下午1点30分左右听到了尖叫声，但决定不报告，因为她认为这只是另一场家庭纠纷。她继续走，完全无视了她所听到的。当伊恩问警察他是否可以拿回玛格丽特的珠宝时，没有珠宝可以给他。她经常戴着一枚钻戒和一块手表，但凶手把它们拿走了。仅那枚戒指就价值2万美元。看起来像是一起抢劫案出了差错。玛格丽特没有敌人，所以这是唯一看起来说得通的事情。当警察得知过去几年家里进行了大规模翻修时，这似乎更说得通了。伊恩无法提供关于到底雇了谁的太多帮助，因为他在工作时，玛格丽特处理了所有这些事情。那么，是不是其中一个技工看中了房子里的东西，决定回来呢？

5
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:59.000
It seemed to fit when you think about the forensic pathologist stating the weapon used looked to be a small hammer or similar tool. Police felt like they might be onto something. There were no records kept of what tradesmen attended, so police got to work questioning as many of them as they could. Builders, carpenters, painters, tillers, plumbers. It all amounted to nothing though. They never tracked down anyone who had completed work in the Edwards home. As good as the theory looked, it wasn't gaining any momentum. Police even spent days searching every hardware store they could find, trying to find a hammer or similar tool that could have inflicted the injuries. It was hoped that if they could identify the tool, it would help narrow down the search for the tradesmen.
当你想到法医病理学家说使用的武器看起来像是一把小锤子或类似的工具时，这似乎很吻合。警察觉得他们可能发现了什么。没有记录显示哪些技工来过，所以警察开始尽可能多地询问他们。建筑商、木匠、油漆工、瓦工、水管工。但这一切都一无所获。他们从未追踪到任何在爱德华兹家完成过工作的人。尽管这个理论看起来不错，但它并没有获得任何进展。警察甚至花了几天时间搜查了他们能找到的每一家五金店，试图找到一把可能造成伤害的锤子或类似工具。人们希望如果他们能确定工具，将有助于缩小对技工的搜寻范围。

6
00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:43.000
But that also amounted to nothing. They couldn't find anything that matched. Ian made an emotional appeal to the media, asking anybody with information to come forward. Photos of the stolen jewellery were also released to the media, in the hope that somebody would recognise them and they would turn up. They were expensive, unique pieces. But this didn't get the police anywhere either. As much as they liked the robbery theory, they couldn't ignore the fact that the majority of murders are committed by somebody close to the victim. Everything suggested Ian and Marguerite were in a loving marriage, with no problems at all. Ian was quoted as saying,
但这同样一无所获。他们找不到任何匹配的东西。伊恩向媒体发出感人呼吁，请求任何有信息的人站出来。被盗珠宝的照片也被发布给媒体，希望有人能认出它们，它们会出现。它们是昂贵、独特的物品。但这也没有让警察取得任何进展。尽管他们喜欢抢劫理论，但他们不能忽视大多数谋杀案都是由受害者身边的人犯下的这一事实。一切都表明伊恩和玛格丽特婚姻美满，没有任何问题。伊恩曾说：

7
00:07:43.000 --> 00:08:35.000
To my knowledge, my wife had no enemies. We had a perfect relationship for the 20 years of our marriage, and we were very much in love. We have three children, and we are very close and happy family. Ian went on to describe Marguerite as happy, graceful, always smiling, always laughing, and never angry. Saying their marriage was perfect bliss. And Ian had an alibi. He was at work the whole day. But it was when police started to look a bit closer, they realised that maybe Ian's alibi wasn't as solid as it initially seemed. Ian's orthodontic surgery was 2.2 kilometres away from the family home, roughly 1.3 miles. Through their investigation, they learnt that Ian was supposed to go home and have lunch with Marguerite the day she was killed.
据我所知，我妻子没有敌人。在我们20年的婚姻中，我们有着完美的关系，我们非常相爱。我们有三个孩子，我们是一个非常亲密和幸福的家庭。伊恩继续描述玛格丽特快乐、优雅，总是微笑，总是大笑，从不生气。说他们的婚姻是完美的幸福。而且伊恩有不在场证明。他整天都在工作。但当警察开始仔细观察时，他们意识到伊恩的不在场证明可能并不像最初看起来那么稳固。伊恩的牙齿矫正诊所距离家2.2公里，大约1.3英里。通过调查，他们得知伊恩本应在玛格丽特被杀那天回家和她一起吃午饭。

8
00:08:35.000 --> 00:09:24.000
But he says he got too busy and had to cancel. Instead, he sent his nurse out to buy him a sandwich. The nurse was out for 25 minutes, and Ian didn't have any patients during that time. So there was a 25 minute window that Ian didn't have an alibi for. Ian was a fit man, who was known to regularly go for a run during his lunch break. Police were able to confirm that his car never left the parking lot of his surgery. Could he have run home, killed Marguerite, and made it back to his surgery in time? Two detectives completed the challenge, running from Ian's surgery to his house, and then back again. Factoring in the time it would have taken to commit the murder.
但他说是他太忙了，不得不取消。相反，他派他的护士出去给他买三明治。护士出去了25分钟，伊恩在那段时间里没有病人。所以有一个25分钟的窗口期，伊恩没有不在场证明。伊恩是一个身体健康的人，众所周知他经常在午休时间跑步。警察能够确认他的车从未离开过诊所的停车场。他能跑回家，杀了玛格丽特，然后及时赶回诊所吗？两名侦探完成了挑战，从伊恩的诊所跑到他家，然后再跑回来。考虑到实施谋杀所需的时间。

9
00:09:24.000 --> 00:10:04.000
And the fact Ian was definitely back seeing a patient straight after lunch, showing no signs he had just been for a run. Police were able to rule it out. They kept an open mind. Ian wasn't ruled out completely, but the idea he physically had anything to do with it was extremely doubtful. That pretty much left them back to square one. The tradesman theory had gotten them nowhere, and Ian didn't look likely. He didn't stop the public's opinion though. Ian felt the suspicious eyes on him everywhere he went. His business partner of 17 years suddenly ended their relationship.
以及伊恩午饭后确实立即回来见病人，没有任何迹象表明他刚跑过步的事实。警察能够排除这种可能性。他们保持开放的心态。伊恩并没有被完全排除，但他与此事有身体接触的想法极其令人怀疑。这几乎让他们回到了原点。技工理论让他们一无所获，伊恩看起来也不太可能。但这并没有阻止公众的舆论。伊恩感到他所到之处都有怀疑的目光。他合作了17年的商业伙伴突然结束了他们的关系。

10
00:10:04.000 --> 00:11:07.000
And people in the area even held dinner parties to sit around and discuss theories about how Ian could have pulled it off. Police freely admitted the investigation had stalled, and it was going cold. It was nine months later, in May 1990, that a $50,000 reward was offered for any information that led to the case being solved. Not only that, the government took the step of offering a pardon to any person who may have assisted, so long as they weren't directly involved in the killing. Police did get plenty of calls and tips and names to check out, but none of it was useful. The case continued to run cold, and it looked destined to remain on the unsolved shelf. But on the 23rd of August 1991, they got the break they were looking for. 35 year old Christopher Anthony Lorenzo was in Long Bay Jail in Sydney, waiting to be sentenced on several armed robbery charges.
该地区的人们甚至举行晚宴，坐在一起讨论伊恩是如何做到的理论。警察坦率地承认调查已经停滞，并且正在变冷。九个月后，即1990年5月，悬赏5万美元征集任何导致案件破获的信息。不仅如此，政府还采取了步骤，向任何可能提供协助的人提供赦免，只要他们没有直接参与杀人。警察确实接到了很多电话、线索和名字需要核实，但都没有用。案件继续变冷，看起来注定要留在未破案件的架子上。但在1991年8月23日，他们得到了他们一直在寻找的突破。35岁的克里斯托弗·安东尼·洛伦佐当时在悉尼的长湾监狱，等待因多项武装抢劫指控被判刑。

11
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:56.000
Lorenzo was born in Cape Town, South Africa, on the 2nd of July 1956. He had a history of drug use, break-ins and armed robberies. Lorenzo had gotten the word out he had information that would be of interest to homicide detectives. They paid him a visit and became very interested in what he had to say when he told them he knew who killed the dentist's wife in Wallara. Prison inmates generally don't give information to police out of the kindness of their heart. There is always a motive, and Lorenzo was no different. He wanted to be moved to a jail that was a bit easier to do time than Long Bay, and he wanted police to have a word to the judges so he could get a reduced sentence for his armed robbery charges.
洛伦佐于1956年7月2日出生在南非开普敦。他有吸毒、入室盗窃和武装抢劫的历史。洛伦佐放出话来，说他有凶杀案侦探会感兴趣的信息。他们拜访了他，当他告诉他们他知道是谁杀了沃拉拉的牙医妻子时，他们变得非常感兴趣。监狱囚犯通常不会出于好心向警察提供信息。总是有动机的，洛伦佐也不例外。他想被转移到一个比长湾更容易服刑的监狱，他希望警察能跟法官说句话，这样他就能减轻武装抢劫指控的刑期。

12
00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:37.000
He was facing a five year sentence, but he didn't want to do that long. Lorenzo had made a handwritten statement for police, detailing everything he knew about Marguerite's murder. This was his story. The day Marguerite was murdered, Lorenzo was at a local pub having lunch and enjoying a few beers. His friend David Anelzac approached him and wanted to borrow his car. It was actually Lorenzo's girlfriend's car, but he agreed. When Anelzac returned the car a few hours later, there was blood in it, and blood on Anelzac himself. Lorenzo asked him what the fuck happened.
他面临五年刑期，但他不想服刑那么久。洛伦佐为警察写了一份手写声明，详细说明了他所知道的关于玛格丽特谋杀案的一切。这就是他的故事。玛格丽特被谋杀的那天，洛伦佐在当地一家酒吧吃午饭，喝了几杯啤酒。他的朋友大卫·阿内尔扎克走近他，想借他的车。其实那是洛伦佐女朋友的车，但他同意了。当阿内尔扎克几个小时后还车时，车里有血，阿内尔扎克自己身上也有血。洛伦佐问他到底发生了什么事。

13
00:12:37.000 --> 00:13:17.000
Anelzac told him he broke into a house, but it went wrong. A woman saw him and started screaming, so he had to silence her. Anelzac pointed out a replica pistol in the boot and told Lorenzo to drown it. But Lorenzo didn't get rid of the gun. He decided to keep it for insurance. While he was cleaning up the blood in the car, he found an expensive looking gold bracelet underneath one of the seats. He decided to keep that too, and he later gave it to his girlfriend. Police believed Lorenzo's story had merit. Anelzac was well-known to them.
阿内尔扎克告诉他，他闯入了一所房子，但出了差错。一个女人看到了他并开始尖叫，所以他不得不让她闭嘴。阿内尔扎克指着后备箱里的一把仿制手枪，告诉洛伦佐把它淹死。但洛伦佐没有处理掉那把枪。他决定留着它作为保险。当他在清理车里的血迹时，他在座位下面发现了一个看起来很昂贵的金手镯。他决定也留着它，后来把它给了他的女朋友。警察认为洛伦佐的故事有价值。阿内尔扎克是他们熟知的人。

14
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:47.000
At the time of Marguerite's murder, he wasn't long out of prison after doing time for a manslaughter charge. But they needed to do some background work to try and verify the story. Lorenzo said he could actually help them with that. He could give police the replica pistol that Anelzac told him to get rid of. In his words, The gun has been right under your nose for years. The armed hold up boys have got it. It's a police exhibit.
在玛格丽特被谋杀时，他因过失杀人罪服刑后刚出狱不久。但他们需要做一些背景工作来试图核实这个故事。洛伦佐说他实际上可以帮助他们。他可以给警察阿内尔扎克告诉他处理掉的那把仿制手枪。用他的话说，这把枪多年来一直就在你们眼皮底下。武装抢劫组的人有它。它是警方的证物。

15
00:13:47.000 --> 00:14:28.000
When Lorenzo was arrested for the armed robberies, police searched his house and took a number of items, including a replica pistol. As Lorenzo's charges weren't finalized and he was still waiting to be sentenced, the replica pistol was still locked away in police evidence. The pistol was immediately sent to forensics to see if they could link it to the murder. And they could. Marguerite's head injuries were a match to the wrist sight on the replica pistol. So the weapon used wasn't a small hammer or similar tool as previously thought. Not only that, the pistol tested positive for blood.
当洛伦佐因武装抢劫被捕时，警察搜查了他的房子并拿走了一些物品，包括一把仿制手枪。由于洛伦佐的指控尚未最终确定，他还在等待判刑，所以仿制手枪仍被锁在警方证据中。手枪立即被送往法医部门，看看他们是否能将其与谋杀案联系起来。他们做到了。玛格丽特的头部伤口与仿制手枪上的准星相符。所以使用的武器并不是之前认为的小锤子或类似工具。不仅如此，手枪的血迹检测呈阳性。

16
00:14:28.000 --> 00:15:07.000
They also managed to track down Lorenzo's girlfriend, Josephine Tapani. Not only did she confirm Lorenzo's story, but she still had the bracelet. It was a bracelet that Marguerite had custom made. Nobody had realized it was missing until Lorenzo gave his story to police. Josephine said it was Lorenzo who actually wore it around initially, but he said it was too tight for him, so he ended up giving it to her. His story was that somebody had given it to him at a takeaway shop in Surrey Hills, a suburb not too far away from Wallara.
他们还设法追踪到了洛伦佐的女朋友约瑟芬·塔帕尼。她不仅证实了洛伦佐的故事，而且她仍然拥有那个手镯。那是玛格丽特定制的手镯。直到洛伦佐向警察讲述他的故事，没有人意识到它不见了。约瑟芬说，最初确实是洛伦佐戴着它，但他说对他来说太紧了，所以他最终把它给了她。他的故事是，有人在萨里山的一家外卖店给了他，萨里山是一个离沃拉拉不太远的郊区。

